## 3. Configuring the AWS CLI

The next task was configuring the AWS Command Line Interface to authenticate through IAM Identity Center.

I ran:

```bash
aws configure sso
```

This command guides the user through configuring an AWS SSO session and a named CLI profile.

After completing the configuration, I checked the available profiles:

```bash
aws configure list-profiles
```

Expected profile:

```text
focusguard-dev
```

I then authenticated:

```bash
aws sso login --profile focusguard-dev
```

The AWS CLI opened a browser authentication flow.

After signing in, I was able to use the configured profile to access AWS.

### Verifying my AWS identity

I ran:

```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity --profile focusguard-dev
```

AWS Security Token Service returned information identifying my authenticated AWS account and assumed role.

This confirmed that the CLI was using the intended AWS identity.

